 4. 🪩 1 for the road: Another Sphere 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Rendering: Courtesy of Prince George's County The Sphere — a 6,000-seat, orb-shaped immersive entertainment venue — got final approval yesterday to be built at Maryland's National Harbor just outside D.C., Axios D.C.'s Cuneyt Dil reports. 

 Local officials are betting that the $1.4 billion mini version of the Las Vegas Sphere will be a big draw. 🏟️ Maryland's Sphere will host immersive concerts and shows with vibrating seats, 4D effects and a 16,000-by-16,000 interior display that the creators say is the "world's highest-resolution LED screen." 

